# Environment (secrets — never commit)
.env

# Spreadsheet inbox, operational GPA data, nothing here is versioned.
# Git used to be the transport for these files (uploaded via the GitHub
# interface, plus `git pull` on the server), which bloated the repo and
# blocked protecting the main branch: import-watch would commit and push on
# its own, and any "require pull request" rule would silently reject that
# push. Now `data/` is a local inbox on the server, fed by scp/rsync or the
# app's /upload screen, and the watcher deletes the spreadsheet after
# importing it.
#
# The whole directory is ignored on purpose, not just *.xlsx: it's a working
# folder, and anything left in it (spreadsheet, image, draft) has no business
# entering the repo. import-watch creates the directory if it doesn't exist.
# Brand images live in public/, which is where the app serves them from.
data/

